{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/kirnbergerii"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kirnbergerII"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two fifths — D→A and A→E — are each narrowed by ½ of the syntonic comma, equal to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"√(20\/9) ≈ 691.202 cents. One fifth — F♯→C♯ — is narrowed by one schisma","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(32805:32768), equal to 16384:10935 ≈ 699.977 cents. The remaining nine fifths are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly because one syntonic comma times one schisma","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equals one Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The two half-comma fifths are unusually flat, giving C-adjacent keys very pure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"thirds while keys with many sharps or flats suffer greatly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Type Property","symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:10IvorTu